# UseBy mobile — local development environment.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file holds names only.
#
# Both are EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables, which Expo inlines into the JS bundle at
# build time. That means they ship inside the app and are readable by anyone
# holding the binary. That is understood and accepted for the value below —
# see the note on the secret.

# Origin of the deployed parse-expiry proxy. Optional: the app falls back to
# the production deployment when this is unset. Point it at a preview
# deployment to test against one without touching code.
EXPO_PUBLIC_USEBY_PROXY_URL=

# The proxy's MOBILE_APP_SECRET, sent as `Authorization: Bearer <value>`.
#
# This is NOT authentication and must not be treated as one. It ships inside a
# distributed mobile binary and can be extracted from it. Its only job is to
# stop the deployment sitting open to anyone who guesses the URL and quietly
# running up the Anthropic bill — a deployment guard, not an identity check.
# It does not identify a user, cannot be revoked per device, and rotating it
# means shipping a new build. It gets replaced by a validated per-user session
# token once real auth exists (decision D4 on the Build Plan).
#
# Without it the app still runs: scanning reports itself as unavailable and the
# user goes straight to manual entry.
#
# For EAS builds set this as an environment variable on the build profile
# instead of shipping a .env file.
EXPO_PUBLIC_USEBY_PROXY_SECRET=
